 "researcher_notes": "Not an existing row: P4447 Northern Loop (14 mi, 24 in, shelved) and P4448 Mainline 100/200 replacement (0.5 mi, 30 in) are different projects. Passes length rule: about 30.2 miles of new pipe per the FERC environmental assessment notice (Federal Register, 5 Aug 2026, docket CP26-19); the EIA August 2026 release says 31 mi (sheet Natural Gas Pipeline Projects, Excel row 88), the company fact sheet says about 25 mi of 36-inch plus about 5 mi of replacement pipe. Replaces about 43 to 50 miles of 1950s pipe, which is abandoned. No added capacity, so capacity left blank. Application filed 10 Nov 2025; EIA target in-service 2028 (company sheet said Q4 2027). Diameter 36 in is the main run; about 5 mi is 30 in. Status proposed (EIA: Applied). FERC, EIA and the company are partly one origin, so independence is limited. Start and end are county level (Mason, Nicholas, Bracken, Pendleton and Campbell Counties KY to Hamilton County OH). No route geometry found. Cost not found. Owner style checked, Columbia Gas Transmission LLC is an exact gazetteer hit; TC Energy is the parent."
